CFile13 - a two-pane file manager on a bootable Kickstart 1.3 floppy
=====================================================================

CFile13 is the Kickstart 1.3 fork of CFile, the keyboard-driven
two-pane file manager for AmigaOS. The main line needs OS 2.04+;
this fork was cut down and back-ported to run on a stock 68000
with Kickstart 1.3 and 1MB of RAM - and to boot straight from
this floppy. Press ? inside the program for the key reference.

Requirements: Kickstart 1.3 (or later), 68000, 1MB RAM - or 512K.

On a 512K machine CFile13 notices and adapts: a 4-colour screen
(same colours, faster blits), smaller buffers, shorter console
scrollback - leaving roughly 40K of working room after boot.
Browsing, copying, viewing, editing and lha archives all work;
LZX packing and zip need more machine (see below).


WHAT WORKS
----------
- Two panes, volume list, full navigation, directory sizes
- Copy / move / delete / rename / new directory, with the
  byte-weighted progress bar
- Marks (all / none / invert), sorting, the / filter
- Text, ANSI and hex viewing; the built-in text editor
- lha and lzx archives: browse inside, view, copy in and out
  (the 68000 builds of both are on this disk)
- ISO 9660 CD images browse like archives, read-only, no OS
  support needed
- find (substring, recursive), bookmarks, directory history
- Protection bits and file comments from the i window
- Icon tooltypes: view AND edit in the editor - written back by
  file surgery, byte-identical except the tooltypes themselves
- RAM disk shows its real free space (free memory), and copies
  into RAM: work - on stock 1.3 it reports itself 100% full
- Swedish keymap (setmap s in the startup; keymap-honest input
  through console.device, so all national keys work)

CFile13 creates T: and ENV: assigns itself (in RAM:) when they
are missing, and removes at exit exactly those it created.
Its config is saved to S:cfile13.config when you change settings.


LIMITATIONS (vs CFile on OS 3.x)
--------------------------------
- No picture or sound viewing (datatypes.library is OS 3.0+),
  no ProTracker playback (ptreplay.library needs OS 2.04+).
  Unknown media hex-views instead.
- No ADF mounting (needs OS 3.2 DAControl). .adf files are
  ordinary files here.
- No automatic pane refresh (no notification in 1.3 filesystems)
  - press F5 to rescan.
- No mark-by-pattern; find is substring-only (no #? wildcards).
- No recursive text search inside files.
- A directory pane holds at most 300 entries (main CFile: 500) -
  more than that and CFile13 says so rather than showing a
  silently shorter list.
- Esc cannot interrupt a running archiver (1.3 Run hides the
  child process) - the operation finishes on its own.
- Zip: extraction via UnZip 5.12 should work but has seen little
  1.3 testing; creating zips is not supported.
- lha on this disk is LhA 1.38 (1992) - the only LhA that runs on
  1.3 (2.x builds need OS 2.0 libraries). It packs and unpacks
  the standard -lh5- method; archives made with the newer -lh6-
  or -lh7- methods will not unpack here.
- LZX CANNOT PACK on a 1MB machine: its encoder needs more free
  memory than remains with CFile13 resident ("Fatal error
  encoding data"), and no option shrinks it enough. Browsing and
  extracting lzx archives is expected to work. Pack with lha -
  which is what an A500 did in 1992 too.
- The shell console for ':' commands opens on the Workbench
  screen and asks for RETURN when done (no AUTO/CLOSE/WAIT in
  the 1.3 console).
- While booted FROM this disk, its own s/startup-sequence cannot
  be saved from inside CFile13 - the boot shell still holds the
  file open ("object in use"; that is AmigaDOS, not a bug).
  Launch with "run >nil: c:cfile13" in the script to avoid it,
  or edit a RAM: copy and copy it back.

Writes to the floppy need the volume validated; if a session was
interrupted mid-write, the next boot revalidates automatically
(l/Disk-Validator is on the disk - do not remove it). Let the
drive settle after a save before quitting an emulator or
ejecting.


THE FILES ON THIS DISK - what may not be removed
-------------------------------------------------
c/cfile13              the program (E, 68000, ~180K)
c/Run, c/Execute       the 1.3 launch road: CFile13 shells
                       through BOTH to run archivers and assigns
c/Assign               the only way to create an assign on 1.3;
                       CFile13 calls it (T:/ENV: self-heal)
c/Stack, c/SetMap,     used by s/startup-sequence (16K stack is
c/Echo                 required; setmap s = Swedish keys)
devs/keymaps/s         the keymap setmap loads
devs/system-configuration  1.3 preferences (pointer, key repeat)
l/Ram-Handler          RAM: does not exist without it
l/Disk-Validator       floppy WRITES fail without it
l/LZX.Keyfile          unlocks the registered LZX
libs/diskfont.library  fonts beyond the ROM Topaz (config FONT)
libs/icon.library      the i window's icon/tooltype rows
s/startup-sequence     echo, stack 16384, setmap s, cfile13

Optional:
c/lha, c/lzx, c/UnZip  the archivers (68000 builds - do not
                       replace with 020+ builds on an A500!)

Removed as dead weight: UNLZX (never called - lzx does it all),
SetMap.info (an icon, and this disk never runs Workbench),
Makedir (CFile13 creates directories through the ROM - n with a
trailing / - and needs no external command for it).


CFile13 is less actively developed than CFile by design: the
feature set freezes at 1.0, fixes are cherry-picked when cheap.
Sources and the full port ledger: the AmigaTools repository,
cfile13/ (see PORT-STATUS.md for what was cut, what was rebuilt
on V33 roads, and why).
